; mirror: the shape joined to its reflection across the seam (SPEC.md §5.4)
mirror[+z] C                                  ; one face: a box twice as tall
half = x[+x&side](1.5) x[+z](2) C              ; a post and half a lintel
mirror[+x&top] half                           ; an arch: the seam is the lintel's end
mirror[-x] half                               ; two faces in one plane: a T
mirror[+x|+z] C                               ; two faces at an angle: the plane runs between them
mirror[+x]{copy} x[+x] C                      ; the copies are made by the step: labelled, and new
x[new](0.5) mirror[+x] x[+x] C
